.TH GOURCE 1
.SH NAME
gource-app \- native Rust source-control history visualizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gource-app
.RB [ --config \ FILE ]
.B view
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gource-app
.RB [ --config \ FILE ]
.B export
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B gource-app
.RB [ --config \ FILE ]
.B diagnose
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gource-app
is the native Rust successor to Gource.  It reads a finite custom log or a
local Git repository directory, builds a bounded canonical history, and
renders an animated directory tree.  The preserved C++ application remains in
the source tree; its historical command-line options are not accepted by this
binary.
.PP
The successor is built with Rust 1.98.1, wgpu, winit, and egui.  The
interactive and non-empty headless paths require a compatible native graphics
adapter and driver.  Headless export means that no window is created; it does
not mean CPU-only portability.
.SH COMMON OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-input\ PATH
Read a regular strict custom-log file, \- for finite standard input, or a local
Git repository directory.  Input is consumed through EOF before an indexed
history is published.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache-dir\ PATH
Opt in to the private persistent indexed-history cache.  Omission disables
persistent caching.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache-bytes\ BYTES
Finite aggregate cache-entry quota.  The default is 4 GiB when caching is
enabled; zero and unbounded sentinel values are rejected.
.TP
.BI \-\-viewport\ WIDTHxHEIGHT
Set the physical viewport.  The default is 1280x720 and each edge is limited to
32,768 pixels.
.TP
.BI \-\-width\ PIXELS \ \-\-height\ PIXELS
Set viewport dimensions as a pair.  Supplying only one is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-seconds-per-day\ SECONDS
Repository seconds represented by one simulated day.  The default is 10.
.TP
.B \-\-realtime
Use real-time repository playback.  This selects the 86,400-seconds-per-day
spelling and conflicts with a different explicit seconds-per-day value.
.TP
.B \-\-no-realtime
Explicitly disable real-time playback.
.TP
.BI \-\-auto-skip-seconds\ SECONDS
Skip idle repository periods longer than the value.  The alias
.BR \-\-auto-skip
is accepted; the default is 3 seconds.
.TP
.BI \-\-time-scale\ FACTOR
Multiply the canonical playback speed.  The default is 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-file-idle-seconds\ SECONDS
Keep deleted files visible for the configured duration.  The alias
.BR \-\-file-idle
is accepted; an unset or zero value disables expiry.
.TP
.BI \-\-camera\ MODE
Select the automatic camera policy, either
.B overview
or
.BR track .
.TP
.BI \-\-seed\ SEED
Set the deterministic layout seed.  The default is 31.
.TP
.BI \-\-filter\ GLOB
Keep events whose repository path matches a glob.  The option may be repeated;
explicit command-line filters replace the configured filter list and any match
is retained.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-record-bytes\ BYTES
Maximum physical record size.  The default is 1 MiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-input-bytes\ BYTES
Maximum finite input size.  The default is 8 GiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-path-bytes\ BYTES
Maximum normalized path size.  The default is 64 KiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-contributor-bytes\ BYTES
Maximum contributor size.  The default is 4 KiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-path-components\ COUNT
Maximum lexical path depth.  The default is 256 components.
.TP
.BI \-\-max-events\ COUNT
Maximum indexed events.  The application default is the maximum u64 value;
choose a smaller value for an explicit event bound.
.TP
.BI \-\-working-memory-bytes\ BYTES
Total parser/index working-memory budget.  The default is 128 MiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-working-disk-bytes\ BYTES
Maximum temporary external-sort disk.  The default is 16 GiB.
.TP
.BI \-\-run-fan-in\ COUNT
Maximum number of sorted runs merged at once.  The default is 32.
.PP
All limits are checked before the relevant operation grows.  A limit failure
is an error, not EOF or silent truncation.
.SH VIEW
.TP
.B gource-app view
Open the native interactive window.  The command accepts the common options.
.PP
The current keyboard controls are:
.BR Space / P
pause or resume;
.BR Right / N
next event;
.B Left
seek one repository second backward;
.BR + / =
and
.B -
raise or halve playback rate;
.BR O , T , M
select overview, track, or manual camera;
.B R
reset the camera; and
.BR Esc / Q
quit.  Left-click selects a point, right-drag pans, and the mouse wheel zooms.
.SH EXPORT
.TP
.BI \-\-output\ PATH
Required destination directory for PNG frames or destination file for video.
The destination must not already exist.
.TP
.B \-\-video
Use the external FFmpeg video sink instead of the PNG frame-directory sink.
.TP
.BI \-\-frame-rate\ RATE
Exact positive frame rate as FPS or NUMERATOR/DENOMINATOR.  The alias
.BR \-\-fps
is accepted; the default is 60.
.TP
.BI \-\-start\ SECONDS
Non-negative repository timestamp at which to start.  The default is zero.
.TP
.BI \-\-end\ SECONDS
Exclusive non-negative repository timestamp at which to stop.  If omitted,
the application uses one second after the final event.
.PP
The schedule uses a fixed 120 Hz replay and an end-exclusive rational frame
schedule.  Every scheduled frame is rendered, including duplicate samples at
the same simulation tick.  PNG export writes deterministic frame names and a
manifest.  Failed or cancelled exports remove private staging artifacts and
do not overwrite an existing destination.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-video ,
FFmpeg is started directly with a fixed argument vector.  Raw RGBA frames are
sent on stdin; FFV1 level 3, intra frames, and Matroska output are requested.
The default queue is three frames with a three-frame byte cap, stderr is capped
at 64 KiB, and the deadline is 30 seconds.  A missing executable, non-zero
exit, timeout, cancellation, or writer error kills and reaps the child and
leaves no final video.  FFmpeg is not bundled or downloaded.
.SH DIAGNOSE
.TP
.BI \-\-threads\ COUNT
Use this many bounded Rayon workers for the parallel replay.  The value must be
non-zero; otherwise available parallelism is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-end\ SECONDS
Stop both measured replays at this repository timestamp.  The alias
.BR \-\-target
is accepted.
.PP
.B gource-app diagnose
parses/indexes once, then measures serial and bounded-parallel replay without
creating a window or GPU context.  It writes one JSON object to standard
output containing
.B ingest_ms ,
.B serial_ms ,
.B parallel_ms ,
.B events ,
.B final_tick ,
.B snapshots_equal ,
and
.B configured_threads .
The command exits successfully only when the final serial and parallel
snapshots compare equal.  Its timings are replay measurements, not end-to-end
render or encoder throughput.
.SH INPUT AND GIT SAFETY
A custom record is
.B timestamp|contributor|A|path
or
.B timestamp|contributor|A|path|#rrggbb
with the corresponding M and D actions.  The finite UTF-8 source is validated
and sorted by (timestamp, source sequence).  Paths are lexical repository
names; they are not opened or used as host filenames.
.PP
When
.BR \-\-input
names a directory, the adapter validates a local directory, snapshots one
revision, and invokes the local Git executable with explicit arguments.  The
final directory must not be a symlink and its identity is rechecked.  The
adapter uses a raw NUL-delimited protocol, disables pagers, replacement
objects, external diffs, text conversion, notes, signatures, rename detection,
and lazy fetch, and bounds stdout, stderr, memory, events, and wall time.  It
never constructs a shell command, fetches from a remote, or publishes a
partial history.  Git is not bundled or downloaded.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.BI \-\-config\ FILE
selects one TOML configuration file.  If it is absent,
.B GOURCE_CONFIG
may select the file.  Precedence is built-in defaults, TOML, known
.B GOURCE_*
environment values, and explicit command-line options.  Paths remain
relative to the process working directory.  The accepted keys and command
sections are documented in
.BR docs/configuration.md .
There is no legacy C++ config loader and no
.BR \-\-load-config
or
.BR \-\-save-config
option in this binary.
.SH CACHE PRIVACY
The cache is used only for regular custom-log files when
.BR \-\-cache-dir
is supplied; stdin and Git-directory inputs bypass persistent cache lookup.
The cache root is owner-private (0700 or an equivalent Windows ACL), entry
files are private, and a bounded lock protects scans and publication.  Keys
include exact input identity, cache/schema versions, ingest options, and
limits.  Entries are checksummed and fully decoded before use.  Corrupt,
stale, or replaced entries are treated as misses or removed safely.  Aggregate
bytes, per-entry bytes, directory-entry count, metadata scan bytes, and staging
state are bounded; writes are private, synchronized, and atomically renamed.
See
.BR docs/cache.md
for the default caps.
.SH NATIVE SUPPORT EVIDENCE
Native packaging scripts build target-qualified archives and smoke the packaged
.B --help
and
.B diagnose
paths.  That evidence does not prove interactive window behavior, GPU
compatibility, or video export on every OS, architecture, driver, or backend.
The corrected headless reference export is a 320x180 Linux llvmpipe Vulkan run
using
.B tests/fixtures/visual-hierarchy-activity.log
and frames 4, 64, and 129 from
.B target/gource-smoke-frames-2 .
Visual review uses the canonical tolerant policy in
.B tests/reference/manifest.toml :
maximum absolute channel delta 8, maximum differing-pixel fraction 0.02, and
no exact PNG hash assertion.  See
.BR docs/export.md
and
.BR docs/releasing.md .
